                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I want to leave a positive review for this game so bad! It has a lot of charm and atmosphere for a horror game. But it's WAY too frustrating and cryptic in both mechanics and story to justify that; especially at the asking price listed. Would give neutral if possible.\n\nIt's a really cool randomly generated maze exploration game, with a decent (if not detail lacking) story for the place. But there is so much trial and error in learning how the game actually plays, unfair infinite regenerating enemy placements that can literally body block you to death (not sure how or why you can't step over a fucking rat...), and every now and then the floor decides to give way and you fall to the next section, massively interrupting exploration progress, making you take a huge chunk of damage, and wasting a ton of time finding a way back.\nThe game also just does not respect your time with the best ending being locked behind New Game+, which contrary to the name doesn't give you jack from the previous playthrough, and instead just disables your map and option to save the damn game, allowing for the unfair crap to end your entire run... horrendous game design. (Though this does add to the dread a bit)\n\nDo think this game is worth a play if your into exploration or ancient horror mysteries. Just be prepared for the slog through waist high bullshit.",
